# Dependency directories
*/node_modules/
/node_modules
**/node_modules
.vscode/
**/coverage/

# Environment variables and anything derived from them.
#
# These patterns have no leading slash, so they match at any depth — backend/.env
# and frontend/.env are covered as well as the root one.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Lockfiles are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# `package-lock.json` used to be listed here, which meant the repository had no
# lockfile at all. Two consequences: every install resolved dependencies afresh,
# so no two environments were guaranteed the same tree (§3.10.2 asks for exactly
# the opposite), and `npm ci` — which the CI pipeline uses and which *requires* a
# lockfile — could never have run.

.vscode

# directories
/example_docs
.DS_Store

# Build output
backend/build
frontend/dist

# Test artefacts
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
